{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals","id":847428,"title":"Lunar Spirit Animals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-14T17:45:24-07:00","id":847428,"title":"Lunar Spirit Animals","content":"So one of my players wants to use an Ox-Dragon as her Lunar mate's Spirit Shape and I could not figure out if that was viable. So the question is how broad are the choices for a Lunar Spirit Shape and what is the difference between a beast and monster (for example a Flame Griffon) by that standard?<br /> Note:I know I can always just allow it but I am curious as to other opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:48:47-07:00","id":847430,"title":"","content":"The ox-dragon is a dinosaur (<i>Triceratops horridus</i>), and thus a real life animal. The Lunar presumably just has to be able to shift into legendary sized animals to take its form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:37:53-07:00","id":847454,"title":"","content":"He'll need the knack for turning into big animals. If he's got that, then it's fine (and it's a starting knack... he'll need a good stamina for it, but that's it).<br /> <br /> What are you going to use for the Lunar rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:28:20-07:00","id":847472,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'd say that if he wants to turn into one that's full sized he needs the knack, but maybe if he doesn't want to take it he can turn into a lesser version? It's definitely a viable option though, or at least it was, even tyrant lizards, yeddim and river dragons were allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:04:18-07:00","id":847488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=847454#post847454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He'll need the knack for turning into big animals. If he's got that, then it's fine (and it's a starting knack... he'll need a good stamina for it, but that's it).<br /> <br /> What are you going to use for the Lunar rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a big concern, she is adamant that she wants a Lunar mate NPC to serve as her Solar's sidekick but I am running into a bit of a wall on converting the rules, truthfully I am stalling till 3e comes out and hoping someone else on the forums converts the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:56:13-07:00","id":847518,"title":"","content":"I converted like, half the rules, but I'm too busy (and uninspired) to finish it.<br /> <br /> Irked did a conversion which is quite good. I don't find it particularly exciting, but it seems well-balanced. One of my players is using it for his Full Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:13:24-07:00","id":847524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=847518#post847518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I converted like, half the rules, but I'm too busy (and uninspired) to finish it.<br /> <br /> Irked did a conversion which is quite good. I don't find it particularly exciting, but it seems well-balanced. One of my players is using it for his Full Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't seem to find it on the forum... what was the thread for the Conversion?<br /> Edit: Nvm found it, thanks for the tip","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-15-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T21:39:03-07:00","id":849134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals#post847428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my players wants to use an Ox-Dragon as her Lunar mate's Spirit Shape and I could not figure out if that was viable. So the question is how broad are the choices for a Lunar Spirit Shape and what is the difference between a beast and monster (for example a Flame Griffon) by that standard?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, 2 things separate &quot;beasts&quot; from &quot;monsters&quot;: Intelligence and mystical powers. <br /> <br /> By my reading of the game, Lunars can only take a spirit-shape of natural, normal (for Creation!) animals, and not ones that actually count as fully sentient, individual people or that have magical powers. So, if it has an Int or Essence over 1, then it probably is off limits, IMO.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T21:53:49-07:00","id":849140,"title":"","content":"Everything under the &quot;animals&quot; header is fair game. Ox-dragons are ordinary triceratopses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T22:32:03-07:00","id":849151,"title":"","content":"What t