oin Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:04:09-07:00","id":849301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=849194#post849194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsupial_lion\" target=\"_blank\"><b>marsupial lion</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (</span></span></span><i>Thylacoleo carnifex</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">)</span></span></span></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo!<br /> <br /> Their hunting strategy is a combination of real life leopards and drop bear folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:35:27-07:00","id":849974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=849151#post849151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'd love to see a Lunar with a Sloth spirit-shape!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suggested one <i>forever</i> ago, remember?<br /> <br /> (I also suggested a trapdoor spider Lunar, and another a queen ant Lunar. I wonder how well a barnacle Lunar could do\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-19-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:22:39-07:00","id":849990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=849974#post849974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggested one <i>forever</i> ago, remember?<br /> <br /> (I also suggested a trapdoor spider Lunar, and another a queen ant Lunar. I wonder how well a barnacle Lunar could do\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>You specialize in grappling. Doesn't matter what you fight you grab on tight and never let go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:40:45-07:00","id":849999,"title":"","content":"I don't see a Barnacle spirit shape being particularly useful-Maybe a deadly beastman if you build it just right right, or as part of a Chimera, and maybe, as nalak42 says, have an aspect that favors grappling related charms in 3E, if tags are still a thing, but actually taking the shape of a tiny nonmoble thingy sounds like suicide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:06:24-07:00","id":850031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=849999#post849999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a deadly beastman if you build it just right right</div> </div> </div> </div>The DBT barnacle Lunar is going to be horrifying, since barnacles have <i>the</i> largest penis-to-body ratio of the animal kingdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=849999#post849999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026but actually taking the shape of a tiny nonmoble thingy sounds like suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you always seem to assume that a Lunar is going to use his spirit shape to fight or hunt or whatever? What if a Lunar's form is a sparrow, a mouse, or a tarantula? You're not going to be killing Dragon-Blooded in that shape, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:44:34-07:00","id":850037,"title":"","content":"Barnacles are amazingly adaptable creatures. I could see the utility of such a form particularly as a smuggler or pirate. Imagine the look on the Wyld Hunts face as they board the boat to chase the Anathema only to find the boat sinking in the middle of the ocean...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:57:34-07:00","id":850038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=850031#post850031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you always seem to assume that a Lunar is going to use his spirit shape to fight or hunt or whatever? What if a Lunar's form is a sparrow, a mouse, or a tarantula? You're not going to be killing Dragon-Blooded in that shape, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but those forms are useful in <i>other</i> ways-as parrow could fly away from trouble that the Lunar can't fight or escape in human form, a mouse is a small and nimble creature that can hid in walls and are also easily overlooked, making them useful for sneaking, and tarrantualas have dark colors, can walk up and down walls, and are much smaller than a person, and are thus similarly suited for stealth. As spirit shapes they are all highly suited for Lunars of the &quot;Tricksters and Seducers&quot; caste( I forget which is which I know full moons are the warriors and hunters)<br /> <br /> A Barnacle, on the other hand, when mature is only mobile when stuck to a boat or whale.<br /> <br /> I mean, the shape would probable have tags for some decent charms, an a Barnacle deadly beast man would be interesting, but an unmodified Barnacle shape is more or less only useful if you need to not let go of something and/or retain water and/or not drown in a situation where you really don't care about being able to move.<br /> <br /> I mean unless you're planning on evolving your Spirit Shape into a legendary monster or incorporating the Barnacle's traits into a Chimera, then rather than use the actual shape you'd be better off using Deadly Beastman or using &quot;Barnacle&quot; as a guideline for the kinds of charms and artifacts you're going to use rather than take it for the actual form itself.<br /> <br /> I could see the Lunar in question having a few a strength charms-&quot;I'm <i>not </i>letting go of you once I've got you in my grasp,&quot; and lots of stamina sharms-stuff to keep you from being moved around maybe? r some of those charms that harden your body or let you grow thick natural armor? And maybe you've got yourself a nice, thick set of artifact armor with evocations that go along a similar theme?<br /> <br /> That I can see, but actually turning into a Barnacle is kind of underwhelming, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T07:55:55-07:00","id":850125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=850031#post850031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DBT barnacle Lunar is going to be horrifying, since barnacles have <i>the</i> largest penis-to-body ratio of the animal kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, barnacles knock off and kill other barnacles by growing quickly. The effect is to either get the rival off the rock, or to crush said rival. One might also imagine that they decorate and rapidly grow on anyone who makes contact with the Lunar, weighing down, immobilizing, and possibly killing them. Presumably, their mobility comes from the human part of the hybrid shape, allowing them a slight bit more freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:57:14-07:00","id":850162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/847428-lunar-spirit-animals?p=850037#post850037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barnacles are amazingly adaptable creatures. I could see the utility of such a form particularly as a smuggler or pirate. Imagine the look on the Wyld Hunts face as they board the boat to chase the Anathema only to find the boat sinking in the middle of the ocean...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not all of them attach to something and not move, check out the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacculina\" target=\"_blank\"> Sacculina </a> genus<br /> <br /> They live inside of crabs. On the left side of the illustration the barnacle's flesh is weaving its way through the entire body of the crab. The bulb under the tail is the egg sack of the parasite. It screws with the crabs brain to take care of it like its own eggs (not it even gets the males to do this)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.oceanographerschoice.com/log/wp-content/IMG_0062.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Here is the inside of a parasitic barnacle that feeds on sharks. Unlike Sacculina it still can easily be seen as a barnacle. It is on the left, the fleshy bulb is the part in the shark. On the right is a normal non parasitic barnacle.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://phenomena.nationalgeographic.com/files/2014/06/Barnacle-comparison.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> One other makes its own float which works for a Lunar who does anything major with ships<br /> <img src=\"http://www.marlin.ac.uk/assets/images/marlin/species/web/o_dosfas.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> A little research makes any animal a good spirit form for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","user":"MuscaDomestica","date":". 03-20-2016, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:57:34-07:00","id":850163,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacculina\" target=\"_blank\">These Barnacles</a> would make better inspiration for demons than Lunars. They are some of the most frightening animals nature every created...if you are a crab.<br /> <br /> Edit: Same Barnacle MuscaDomestica posted about. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:06:24-07:00","id":850170,"title":"","content":"I would think parasite Barnacles would be a different shape from normal Barnacles, possibly belonging to a demonblooded or wyld-tainted mortal who then exalted as a lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}